WEBVTT

00:00:09.666 --> 00:00:12.333
Welcome to my warehouse.

00:00:12.416 --> 00:00:13.875
Oh, my God, I love your dress.

00:00:13.958 --> 00:00:15.958
Oh! Thank you.

00:00:16.041 --> 00:00:17.333
[grunts] Fru Fru and I

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:20.333
are now equal partners
in the family business.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:24.916
She brings wonderful ideas
for crime and for fashion

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.416
while I get more time to focus
on what matters most:

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.291
being grandpapa
to my little Judith.

00:00:32.375 --> 00:00:34.041
Kiss my ring.

00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:35.041
[chuckles]

00:00:35.125 --> 00:00:36.166
Kiss the stinkin' ring
right now!

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:37.291
You kiss it right now!
Kiss it!

00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:39.166
Mwah.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.875
Nonno
, you said we were gonna

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:43.375
make cement shoes
for Mr. Weaselton.

00:00:43.458 --> 00:00:45.333
Oh, that's my girl.

00:00:45.416 --> 00:00:47.041
They grow up so fast.

00:00:47.125 --> 00:00:49.250
-You shut your mouth, fox!
-You run your mouth too much!

00:00:50.208 --> 00:00:52.250
Anyways, you're in trouble.

00:00:52.333 --> 00:00:55.958
And we like one of yas,
so we're here to help.

00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:58.500
New clothes. New identities.

00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:00.500
Truck out of town
leaves in an hour.

00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:02.708
And your meter maid cart
is taken care of.

00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:06.291
[inhales]

00:01:06.375 --> 00:01:08.125
I think you misunderstand.

00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:10.333
We've been framed
by the lynxes.

00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:11.583
And an innocent snake needs...

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:13.916
Judy, the lynxes
are killers...

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.125
[grunts]
...and they have no honor.

00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:19.333
And this Tundratown expansion

00:01:19.416 --> 00:01:21.708
only makes them
more dangerous.

00:01:21.791 --> 00:01:26.041
Territorial animals will do
anything for more land.

00:01:26.125 --> 00:01:27.833
So, if whatever
you're tangled up in

00:01:27.916 --> 00:01:31.291
threatens their plans,
you're dead.

00:01:31.375 --> 00:01:34.708
You don't fight the cats.
You leave.

00:01:34.791 --> 00:01:37.875
Sir, I know you're trying
to look out for us.

00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:40.625
But we took an oath
to protect this city.

00:01:40.708 --> 00:01:42.416
And justice doesn't run.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.916
On behalf of myself,

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.208
"Rick Wilde,"
and "Miss Trudy Cabbagepatch,"

00:01:48.291 --> 00:01:50.458
we thank you for your truck
to salvation and-- Ow!

00:01:50.541 --> 00:01:51.625
We cannot accept your offer.

00:01:51.708 --> 00:01:53.375
We are helping that snake.

00:01:53.458 --> 00:01:55.083
Boy, you're really
tossing that "we" around.

00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:56.458
Snakes may have been framed

00:01:56.541 --> 00:01:57.791
for the fanging
of that tortoise.

00:01:57.875 --> 00:01:59.541
Do you have any idea why?

00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:02.000
Or how this book
could prove it?

00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:03.583
I wish I did.

00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:06.333
But if it has to do
with snakes,

00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:09.416
your best bet
is talking to a reptile.

00:02:10.166 --> 00:02:11.791
Do you know any?

00:02:12.375 --> 00:02:13.958
Almost no one does.

00:02:14.041 --> 00:02:18.166
They keep to themselves,
hide out in Marsh Market.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.083
But you can still find 'em.

00:02:20.166 --> 00:02:22.583
You just need
a reptile expert.

00:02:22.666 --> 00:02:25.125
Someone local
who knows where to go.

00:02:25.208 --> 00:02:27.125
Lucky for you, I met someone.

00:02:27.208 --> 00:02:28.416
She runs a podcast!

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.250
PODCASTER NIBBLES MAPLESTICK
SCALES & TALES OF THE WEIRD

00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:33.250
[Nick] No, no. Trudy Cabbagepatch,
Rick Wilde says no.

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:36.166
[Nibbles] Oh, yeah!

00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:39.458
If Hopps and Wilde
are on the lam,

00:02:39.541 --> 00:02:42.333
subtle sleuthin' 'tis my jam.

00:02:42.416 --> 00:02:44.291
Woo! Mind the splinters.

00:02:44.375 --> 00:02:45.916
Oh, you called
the right beaver.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:49.041
If you wanna talk to
a reptile, I am your gal.

00:02:49.125 --> 00:02:50.833
Also, if you need to talk
to a jackalope,

00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:53.708
which are real, Mom!

00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:56.208
[chuckles]
Excuse us. Team meeting.

00:02:56.291 --> 00:02:57.791
Vetoing the beave.

00:02:57.875 --> 00:03:00.333
New vote: All in favor
of "Truck to Being Alive

00:03:00.416 --> 00:03:03.125
and Laying Low Till This
Blows Over-ville"? I mean...

00:03:03.208 --> 00:03:05.125
Hopps and Wilde
do not bail on a case.

00:03:05.208 --> 00:03:06.291
But she's crazy.

00:03:06.375 --> 00:03:08.833
Probably lead poisoning
from eating too many pencils.

00:03:11.666 --> 00:03:12.791
Do you know a reptile who can

00:03:12.875 --> 00:03:14.041
tell us the hidden secret
in here,

00:03:14.125 --> 00:03:15.791
or why the lynxes
framed the snakes?

00:03:16.416 --> 00:03:17.583
[sighs]

00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:19.833
Twenty-four hours.
Sunrise tomorrow.

00:03:19.916 --> 00:03:21.875
If we strike out,
then we go into hiding,

00:03:21.958 --> 00:03:23.333
and "Judy Cabbagepatch" it is.

00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:24.250
[horn honks]

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.750
[groans]

00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:27.583
It's "Trudy" Cabbagepatch,

00:03:27.666 --> 00:03:29.083
and the safe word
is "coconut."

00:03:29.166 --> 00:03:31.458
In the darkness
of a dank underpass,

00:03:31.541 --> 00:03:32.958
they stepped into the vehicle,

00:03:33.041 --> 00:03:36.500
not realizing their lives
were about to change.

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.750
Because we're gonna
meet a reptile?

00:03:38.833 --> 00:03:40.916
Because you're about to be
best buds

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:43.875
with Nibbles Maplestick!

00:03:43.958 --> 00:03:47.541
Takes two to tango, but
a threesome to be somethin'.

00:03:47.625 --> 00:03:51.041
Let's find you a reptile
and romp the swamp.

00:03:58.541 --> 00:03:59.416
[inhales]

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.250
Breathe it in!

00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:02.750
-[Judy] Oh!
-[Nibbles whoops]

00:04:06.416 --> 00:04:08.041
[Nibbles] Now, if any reptile
would know

00:04:08.125 --> 00:04:10.291
the secret of that book
and why the snake wants it...

00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:12.250
-Hey, Johnny!
-[Johnny] Oh, no!

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:14.750
...it's my old lizard friend,
Jesús.

00:04:14.833 --> 00:04:17.916
[Judy] Why would a lizard
hide here?

00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:21.625
Well, when Zootropolis
was founded,

00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:23.625
the whole neighborhood
got cut off

00:04:23.708 --> 00:04:25.000
from the rest of the town.

00:04:25.083 --> 00:04:26.458
Kinda on our own here.

00:04:26.541 --> 00:04:27.375
[grunting]

00:04:27.458 --> 00:04:29.625
Yeah, that's probably why
reptiles like it.

00:04:29.708 --> 00:04:31.375
They can just do their thing.

00:04:31.458 --> 00:04:32.833
Plus, it's the only place
in town

00:04:32.916 --> 00:04:35.875
you can get away with
wearing a shirt and no pants.

00:04:35.958 --> 00:04:37.958
Loving tour time
with Woodchuckles.

00:04:38.041 --> 00:04:39.458
-[whispers] Great call.
-[Judy growls]

00:04:39.541 --> 00:04:41.083
-We need her.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:41.166 --> 00:04:42.166
Like a hole in the head.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:43.166
[dolphin squawks]

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:44.916
Bad timing. Hmm.

00:04:45.541 --> 00:04:47.750
Okay, to get to
Jesús's hideout,

00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:49.333
we gotta take a ferry.

00:04:49.416 --> 00:04:50.750
Just let me handle the locals.

00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:53.583
Water folk tend to be a little
standoffish around landies.

00:04:53.666 --> 00:04:56.083
Well, I've been hustling
the streets since I was 12.

00:04:56.166 --> 00:04:58.375
I think I can handle
a juggling seal.

00:04:58.458 --> 00:05:00.375
-[roars]
-Oh! [chuckles]

00:05:00.458 --> 00:05:02.291
Sea lion.

00:05:02.375 --> 00:05:03.458
He's not from around here.

00:05:03.541 --> 00:05:05.000
-But coin's a coin.
-[growling]

00:05:05.083 --> 00:05:08.833
Oh, no. Change... [grunts]
...is a choking hazard.

00:05:08.916 --> 00:05:11.583
-Well, honest mistake.
-[roars]

00:05:11.666 --> 00:05:13.583
Do not do that!

00:05:13.666 --> 00:05:15.208
Let's let Nibbles handle this.

00:05:15.291 --> 00:05:16.791
[Nibbles] Thank you, Judith.

00:05:16.875 --> 00:05:19.416
Conversing with these
beautiful sea creatures

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.416
is like talking to anyone
a little different.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:25.041
Just takes open
and respectful communication.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:27.583
[ringing]

00:05:27.666 --> 00:05:28.666
[bubbling]

00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:34.708
-Heya, bub.
-Hey, bub.

00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:36.083
-Heya, bub, hey.
-Hey, bub, heya.

00:05:36.166 --> 00:05:37.333
-Bubba, bubba, bubba.
-Bubba, bubba, bubba.

00:05:37.416 --> 00:05:39.333
-Heya, bub.
-Hey, bub. Hey, bub, bub.

00:05:39.416 --> 00:05:41.500
-Heya, bub. Bubby, bub.
-Hey, bub. Hey, bub. Hey, ho.

00:05:41.583 --> 00:05:42.500
-Heya, bub, bub.
-Hey, bub.

00:05:43.541 --> 00:05:44.583
Seen Jesús?

00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:45.666
Yup.

00:05:52.125 --> 00:05:53.916
And now we leave town.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.000
-[rumbling]
-[Judy yelps]

00:05:59.916 --> 00:06:01.083
[double whistle]

00:06:01.166 --> 00:06:02.166
Eh?

